Docs claim TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS gates cookies:
README.md:257:When no proxy is configured, the default trust list (`127.0.0.1`) ensures forwarded headers are only honored from localhost.
SECURITY.md:24:- **Session cookies** -- browser sessions are signed, HTTP-only, SameSite=Lax cookies with a 30-day max age. Cookies are marked secure when the request is HTTPS or carries `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` from an IP in `TRUSTED_PROXY_IPS`; configure that trust list so forwarded headers are only honored from expected proxies.
